{
  "_why": "Which tools are registered as typed MCP tools (tier1) and which are reachable only through the tier-2 discovery layer (search_revit_api / query_revit_registry / send_code_to_revit). Tier-1 tools cost tool-surface tokens in EVERY session before any work happens; tier-2 entries cost zero, because the corpus lives in revit_function_registry.json, not in a tool schema.",
  "_tier2_criterion": "A tool is tier-2 if the Revit-side command it sends has no C# handler in commandset/. Registering such a tool advertises a capability that cannot execute: it spends context, competes for the model's tool choice, and fails at the bridge. All 69 tier-2 entries below are already described in revit_function_registry.json with verification_status 'unimplemented', so the model can still discover them and fall back to send_code_to_revit.",
  "_promotion_rule": "Move a name from tier2 to tier1 in the same change that adds its C# command handler to commandset/ and its entry to command.json. tests/tool_tiers.test.mjs enforces the invariant, so a promotion without a handler fails the suite.",
  "_planned_gap_tools": "revit_function_registry.json also carries ~163 tier:3/verification_status:'planned' entries, identified by diffing this connector's tool set against REVIT_MCP_study (a separate, fully-implemented Revit MCP project) to find genuine capability gaps — tools already covered by this repo's generic create_line_based_element/create_point_based_element/create_surface_based_element/place_family_instance/ai_element_filter tools were deliberately NOT added, to avoid duplicating functionality this repo already exposes more generically. Those entries are intentionally NOT listed in tier1/tier2 here: tier2 in this file specifically means 'a real server.tool() TS definition exists, only the C# handler is missing' (enforced by tests/tool_tiers.test.mjs's ghost check), and none of these 163 have a TS file yet. A 'planned' entry graduates to tier2 the same day someone writes its TS tool file + zod schema (even with a stub/no-op handler); it graduates from tier2 to tier1 only once commandset/ also has a working C# handler.",
